# ---> Go
# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

/t
*.bak

# Keystone Core binaries (built via make build into build/, but catch strays in root)
/kscore-*
/kscorectl
/trackerctl
/promogen

# Keystone Core specific
build/
dist/
docvalidation
scripts/docvalidation/docvalidation
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
kscore-agent.yaml
*.creds
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
.DS_Store
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
coverage.out
# CI captures the test suite's output here so a failure can be
# recovered from an artifact; job logs are not API-readable.
test-output.log
.idea

# Rust build artifacts.
#
# `target/` is scoped to the repository root. As `**/target/` it matched any
# directory named target anywhere, which is not a build-output pattern but a
# name collision: Generation 1's `internal/cli/target/` was a Go source package,
# and `required_test.go` written into it on 2026-09-04 was ignored from the
# moment it was created. It reached no commit on any branch, including the
# archive, and survived only as an untracked file in a working tree until P11a
# removed it.
#
# The risk was not historical. Generation 2's journeys are about targeting an
# agent, so a `target` package is a plausible thing for a C task to create — and
# it would have been invisible to `git status` and skipped by `git add -A`.
/target/
Cargo.lock
!modules/sdk/rust/Cargo.lock

# C++ build artifacts
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles/
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/Makefile.cmake
**/*.cmake
!**/CMakeLists.txt

# WASM build artifacts
*.wasm
*.wat

# Hugo documentation
docs/.hugo_build.lock
docs/node_modules
docs/package-lock.json
docs/resources
docs/public

# E2E test reports
test/e2e/performance/reports/
/reports/
/internal/loadtest/reports/
/.python-version

# Claude Code / AI session artifacts
CHECKPOINT.md
.claude-session-notes.md
.claude/
!.claude/commands/
SESSION-SUMMARY*.md
*_TEST_RESULTS.md
*_SESSION*.md
.claude-session-context.md
tools/moddoc/moddoc

# Build cache
.cache/

# A `go build` inside a nested tool module drops a binary named after its
# directory. Ignore that shape generally rather than listing tools by hand —
# the hand-written list missed capcheck the moment it became a module.
/tools/capcheck/capcheck
/tools/transition/transition
bin/
